                                            <h2 class="type-h3">Johnny Daukes</h2>

                                                                                            <p class="type-h5">Writer</p>
                                                                                    </div>

                                        <div class="person-dialog__bio margin-trim type-body-l">
                                            <p>Johnny Daukes is a writer, filmmaker and musician whose career has moved restlessly between film, television, radio, comedy and music.<u></u><u></u></p>
<p>He began his career editing music videos in Soho before becoming one of the voices of Channel 4’s <em>Eurotrash</em>, a role he continued for 16 series and which led to a parallel career as a voice artist that continues today. In the 1990s he fronted indie bands FIN and SENNA before moving into comedy writing, winning the BBC Greenlight Award and creating work including <em>Radio9</em>, <em>The Message</em>, <em>The Scanner</em> and two series of <em>Cracking Up</em> for BBC Radio 4.<u></u><u></u></p>
<p>As a filmmaker, Daukes wrote and directed the BIFA-nominated feature <em>Acts of Godfrey</em>, starring Simon Callow, Harry Enfield and Celia Imrie. His editing credits include <em>Finding Your Feet</em>, <em>Fisherman’s Friends</em>, <em>Settlers</em>, <em>Fisherman’s Friends 2</em> and <em>Mother’s Pride</em>.<u></u><u></u></p>
<p>He has released several critically acclaimed albums, including <em>Promise</em>, named Sunday Times Album of the Week, and in 2022 published his memoir, <em>Shadowman: Records of a Life Corrupted</em>.<u></u><u></u></p>

                                        </div>
