                        <div class="person__header">
                            <h3 class="type-h6">Jessica McKenna</h3>

                                                            <p class="type-body-s">Director</p>
                            
                            <div class="person__header__flex">
                                
                                                            </div>
                        </div>

                                                    <template data-dialog-content="dialog-person-4-8762">
                                <article class="person-dialog">
                                    
                                    <div class="person-dialog__content">
                                        <div class="person-dialog__header margin-trim">
                                            <h2 class="type-h3">Jessica McKenna</h2>

                                                                                            <p class="type-h5">Director</p>
                                                                                    </div>

                                        <div class="person-dialog__bio margin-trim type-body-l">
                                            <p>Jessica is a director across professional and participatory theatre. They trained at the Royal Central School of Speech and Drama and Morley College. As Director, Jessica’s credits include <i>Half Time</i> and <i>Fifteen Minutes</i> (Almeida), <i>Embrace</i> and<wbr /> <i>Outside</i> (Arcola), <i>Crawl</i> (The Glitch) and <i>The Prophetic Visions of Bethany Lewis</i> (The Other Palace and Brighton Fringe). As Assistant/Associate Director, their credits include <i>Here Comes J. Edgar!</i> (King&#8217;s Head Theatre), <i>Lovestuck</i> (Theatre Royal Stratford East), <i>The Recoverist Theatre Project</i> (Southwark Playhouse) and <i>The Key Workers Cycle</i> (Almeida). <span>Jessica is Lead Artist for Arcola’s Queer Collective, and deliver participatory theatre projects across London with the Almeida, Go Live, Jacksons Lane, The Old Vic and Tender Education &amp; Arts.</span></p>

                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </article>
                            </template>
                                            </li>
                                                                                                                                        
                    <li class="person not-prose no-image has-grey-background-color">
                                                                                    <button class="btn btn--square person__dialog-trigger btn--grey"
                                    data-dialog-open="people-4"
                                    data-dialog-content-template="dialog-person-4-6279">
                                    <span class="sr-only">Open Bio for Robert Innes Hopkins</span>
                                    <div class="btn__icon">
                                        <div class="mask-icon"
                                            style="--icon--url: url('/wp-content/themes/arcola-theatre-theme/public/images/plus.svg')"></div>
                                    </div>
                                </button>
                                                    
                        <div class="person__header">
                            <h3 class="type-h6">Robert Innes Hopkins</h3>

                                                            <p class="type-body-s">Designer</p>
                            
                            <div class="person__header__flex">
                                
                                                            </div>
                        </div>

                                                    <template data-dialog-content="dialog-person-4-6279">
                                <article class="person-dialog">
                                    
                                    <div class="person-dialog__content">
                                        <div class="person-dialog__header margin-trim">
                                            <h2 class="type-h3">Robert Innes Hopkins</h2>

                                                                                            <p class="type-h5">Designer</p>
                                                                                    </div>

                                        <div class="person-dialog__bio margin-trim type-body-l">
                                            <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Theatre credits include: </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Stage Kiss</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Hampstead Theatre), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Anne Boleyn The Musical</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Hever Castle), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">All’s Well That Ends Well, Pericles, Julius Caesar, Anthony and Cleopatra, Titus Andronicus, Coriolanus, Don Quixote, Oppenheimer</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (RSC),</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Neville’s Island, Speed the Plow, </span></i><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Clybourne Park </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(West End), <em>Dear Jack, Dear Louise, </em></span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Cry Baby, Kenny Morgan</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Arcola), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Other Desert Cities </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Old Vic), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Crucible, Swallows and Amazons</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Bristol Old Vic), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">King Lear </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Chichester </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">Festival Theatre/BAM).</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Opera credits include: </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Die Fledermaus </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Opera Theatre St. Louis),</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> La Traviata</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (LA </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">Opera, US), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Tamerlano, Belshazzar</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (The Grange Festival),</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Parsifal, Tristan und Isolde, Tosca</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (San Francisco Opera), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">La Traviata</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (San Francisco Opera), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Brand New </span></i><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Orchestra Shell, Siegfried, Das Rheingold, Die Walküre, Rigoletto</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Lyric Opera </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">Chicago), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">In Parenthesis, War and Peace, Rigoletto, Flying Dutchman</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Welsh National </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">Opera).</span></p>

                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </article>
                            </template>
